---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About" current="about">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Bioregional Intelligence — Catalunya</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      A static dashboard that makes Catalunya's regenerative ecosystem legible to the public.
      Cohort showcases, actor and network maps, and bioregional-health indicators — combined into a
      single readable surface.
    </p>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>
      Catalunya hosts a dense, networked regenerative ecosystem — cooperatives, research institutes, rural initiatives, urban commons, finance experiments. Most of this work isn't legible from outside it. This dashboard is a public-facing layer that surfaces what's happening, who's doing it, and where it lives.
    </p>

    <h2>What's here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cohorts</strong> — public showcases of project cohorts. The first is Regenerant Catalunya, the GG24 local funding round.</li>
      <li><strong>Actors</strong> — the ecosystem-network view (the broader actor map ported from `refi-bcn-os`). Coming next.</li>
      <li><strong>Indicators</strong> — bioregional-health signals across Catalunya. In development.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      All content is YAML-canonical, hand-curated, and published openly. The data layer is auditable in the source repo. Map layers are simplified comarques GeoJSON from the Generalitat de Catalunya (ODbL).
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      Code: MIT. Content: CC BY-SA 4.0. Re-use freely with attribution.
    </p>

    <h2>Built by</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://refibcn.cat">ReFi Barcelona</a>, in dialogue with the broader Catalan regenerative ecosystem. Source on <a href="https://github.com/luizfernandosg/bioregional-intelligence">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
.prose {
  max-width: 38rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 4rem 2rem;
}
.prose .lede {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  color: var(--rule);
}
.prose h2 {
  margin-top: 2rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule);
  padding-top: 1rem;
}
.prose ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
.prose li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
